{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\fs22 Requirements Table - Lab 1\line Problem Statement #47: Domain & SSL Certificate Expiry Alert System\line\line FR-001 | Functional | High\line Description: The system shall initiate TLS handshakes against monitored domains daily, extract certificate expiration dates, and trigger alerts at 30, 15, and 3 days before expiry.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if alerts are generated at 30, 15, and 3 days before certificate expiry; fail if an alert is missing or uses the wrong threshold.\line Rationale: Implements the core certificate-expiry monitoring requirement.\line\line FR-002 | Functional | High\line Description: The system shall perform daily WHOIS lookups for monitored domains and identify domain registration expiration dates.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if WHOIS data and registration expiry are stored for every monitored domain; fail if data is missing or stale after a successful lookup.\line Rationale: Domain expiration is a separate availability and security risk.\line\line FR-003 | Functional | Medium\line Description: The system shall allow a SysAdmin to add, edit, delete, and view the list of monitored domains and SSL endpoints.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if saved changes are reflected in the monitored list and next audit; fail if changes are missing or unintended endpoints remain.\line Rationale: Accurate monitoring scope is required.\line\line FR-004 | Functional | High\line Description: The system shall escalate expiry alerts through the configured escalation ladder until acknowledged or the final escalation level is reached.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if each configured level is reached when unacknowledged; fail if a level is skipped or escalation stops prematurely.\line Rationale: Ensures time-critical warnings reach responsible personnel.\line\line FR-005 | Functional | Medium\line Description: The system shall provide a dashboard showing current domain and certificate expiry status, upcoming expirations, audit results, and alert history.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if current status loads and filtering/searching works correctly; fail if status is stale, missing, or filtering is incorrect.\line Rationale: Provides operational visibility.\line\line NFR-001 | Nonfunctional - Performance & Scalability | High\line Description: The monitoring engine shall scan a list of 1,000 domains and SSL endpoints in under 3 minutes.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if benchmarking completes 1,000 endpoints in under 3 minutes; fail otherwise.\line Rationale: Supports timely daily audits as the environment grows.\line\line NFR-002 | Nonfunctional - Security | High\line Description: The system shall store credentials and other sensitive monitoring configuration securely using encryption and least-privilege access controls.\line Acceptance Criteria: Pass if secrets are encrypted at rest and in transit and only authorized roles can access them; fail if plaintext storage or unauthorized access is possible.\line Rationale: Protects operational credentials and sensitive monitoring data.\line}